        <mxCell id="backToPool" value="→ back into the pool for another courier" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;fontColor=#c2410c;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="725" width="320" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-gate" value="Why it takes two parties:

A courier pressing &quot;collected&quot; is only their word for it.
Until the shop confirms, nobody has actually taken the
parcel — so it is not treated as collected, and the
customer is not given anybody’s number.

The one exception: the shop being asked to confirm sees
the courier’s name from the moment they ask, because it
is being asked to verify that this person took it." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="980" y="140" width="360" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-race" value="Claiming is a single conditional update, so two couriers
racing for the same parcel cannot both win. The second
is told somebody got there first." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="980" y="330" width="360" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
